                    <head>Compactata Iglaviensia</head>
                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc form="codex">
                            <supportDesc>
                                <extent>
                                    <measure type="leftFlyleaves" unit="folios"/>
                                    <measure type="rightFlyleaves" unit="folios"/>
                                </extent>
                            </supportDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <additions>
                            <p>
                                <locus from="Envelope_1r" to="Envelope_1r" scheme="other"/>
                                <note>In brown ink by a modern hand (possibly <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102528">Henrik Aminson</persName>): <quote>21. Compactata Iglaviensia. ed. Matth. Collinus. Mns.</quote></note>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <locus from="Envelope_1v" to="Envelope_1v" scheme="other"/>
                                <note>In pencil by <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102787">
                                        Mats
                                        Åmark</persName>: <quote>Förseglingen öppnad af undertecknad i april 1930, som efter mycket letande och efterforskningar återfann detta MS i en bunt katalogfragment i Domkyrkobiblioteket. Mats Åmark Bibliotekarie Dky Bibl.</quote></note>
                            </p>
                        </additions>
                        <bindingDesc>
                            <binding contemporary="true">
                                <p>The original covers are lost. On <locus from="Spine" to="Spine" scheme="other"/>: a blue  19th century paper strip. The volume is kept in a paper envelope, placed in a modern cardboard box with marbled paper covers.</p>
                                <p>
                                    <dimensions type="binding">
                                        <height quantity="150" unit="mm"/>
                                        <width quantity="95" unit="mm"/>
                                        <depth quantity="3" unit="mm"/>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </p>
                            </binding>
                        </bindingDesc>
                    </physDesc>
                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <p>
                                <origPlace cert="high">
                                    <placeName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/place/100211">Bohemia</placeName>
                                </origPlace>
                            </p>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>According to <bibl>
                                    <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107610" type="short">Callmer (1977)</title>
                                    <citedRange unit="page" from="121" to="121"/>
                                </bibl>, the manuscript belonged to the library of Rudolf II at Prague castle, but this cannot be proved with certainty. </p>
                            <p>The manuscript is listed in <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102783">Vossius</persName>' catalogue from <date when="1751"/> (<orgName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/org/100004">National Library of Sweden</orgName> MS U 202:1, p. 173) as <quote>Iglaviensium Compactatorum Expositio</quote>, which strongly suggests that it was brought to <placeName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/place/100081">Sweden</placeName> as spoils of war. </p>
                            <p>It was misplaced in the early 20th century, but found among catalogue fragments in <orgName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/org/100009">Strängnäs Cathedral Library</orgName> by <persName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/person/102787">Mats Åmark</persName> in <date when="1930"/>, see <bibl>
                                    <title ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/bibl/107611" type="short">Veselá (2025)</title>
                                    <citedRange unit="page" from="186" to="187"/>
                                </bibl> and literature quoted there.</p>
                        </provenance>
                        <acquisition>
                            <p>To <orgName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/org/100009">Strängnäs Cathedral Library</orgName> from the <orgName ref="https://www.manuscripta.se/org/100004">Royal Library</orgName> ca <date when="1652"/>.</p>
                        </acquisition>
                    </history>
